1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,120
Your blood vessels could
wrap around Earth twice.

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:06,278
Inside your body is a hidden network
of arteries, veins and capillaries.

3
00:00:06,358 --> 00:00:10,138
Line them all up end to end, and they'd
stretch over sixty thousand miles.

4
00:00:10,218 --> 00:00:13,692
Earth's equator is only about
twenty-five thousand miles around.

5
00:00:13,772 --> 00:00:16,953
So one human could circle
the entire planet more than twice.

6
00:00:17,033 --> 00:00:20,318
And that's a child. Scientists
estimate an adult has even more.

7
00:00:20,398 --> 00:00:23,524
Most of that length is capillaries,
the tiniest vessels of all.

8
00:00:23,604 --> 00:00:25,144
You might have around ten billion of them.

9
00:00:25,224 --> 00:00:28,128
Here's the wild part: all of it
fits inside you right now.

10
00:00:28,208 --> 00:00:31,294
Thousands of miles of tubing,
folded into a single body.

11
00:00:31,374 --> 00:00:34,676
Twice around the planet, and it's
all inside you. Follow for more.

